  "review_findings_addressed": [
    {
      "id": "LAST-SOURCE-R5-01",
      "change": "Keep true authentication_state USABLE for a current valid credential. Empty current Source authority maps to existing authorization_state EXPIRED when nonrevoked Sources have naturally expired and no live Source remains; otherwise REVOKED_CONNECTION. Never fabricate NONE or extend the architecture enum/invariants.",
      "actual_proof": "Existing final-Source-expiry, final Context grant revoke and original membership revoke cases now call actual evaluate and status; assert valid true, empty reason_codes/capabilities, USABLE authentication, proper EXPIRED/REVOKED_CONNECTION, complete authorization and Integration business snapshots unchanged, and no new diagnostic rows or receipt/event."
    },
    {
      "id": "LAST-SOURCE-R5-02",
      "change": "Entrance check retained. Private cores recheck current Source after real Request/claim/I locks and before mutation/materialization; ready verification uses its own I SHARE path. Request INSERT unique-key waits are rechecked in both result branches without changing FOUND before the old decision. Bind refreshes current identity/authority/live after waits at steps6/7. All seven public business callers recheck outside core exception blocks after core return, so later waits and authority loss roll back the entire RPC including pending/rejected receipts. Initial vs final current effective projection comparison also rejects partial narrowing instead of committing old write authority. Status, revoke and Native/raw branches retain control semantics.",
      "actual_proof": "14 actual controlled lock-wait vectors: seven public families crossed independently with a real Native last-membership revoke and natural Source deadline passing while the backend is proven blocked; exact42501 denial and all authorization/Integration/Request/identity/claim/fact/declaration/verification/link/ownership/revoke/reauth/receipt/event/diagnostic effects unchanged. Two additional partial-loss waits retain real read, reject source_permission_changed_during_call, fully roll back their RPC and prove actual MCP read remains admitted/write denied."
    }
  ],
